Shared Web Reconciliation / Compatibility Verification ΓÇö corrected Owner credential boundary

Result: COMPATIBLE_FOR_PLANNING / NO CONCRETE WEB INCOMPATIBILITY / NO IMPLEMENTATION AUTHORITY.

Shared Web consumes Application comment `5291019787` and accepts the corrected planning semantics:

- bare FSATS subscription does not require user API/broker credentials;
- advisory/non-execution use, including the user AI conversational advisory experience, does not require user API/broker credentials;
- user-supplied broker/API credentials are introduced only when the user explicitly opts into an Automated Trading / execution capability that actually requires them;
- Automated Trading enablement remains a separate governed stage from subscription/advisory use;
- Trading Execution consumes governed user broker-execution credential references for automated execution;
- no ordinary advisory user is required to provide FSAPMA provider/service credentials merely to use consultation/analysis/recommendation features;
- Web may display only authoritative non-secret readiness/lifecycle metadata and shall not treat credential submission as acceptance or execution authority;
- exact secret storage, transfer, validation, schema, and runtime binding remain future governed work.

The current Web conversational design is compatible with this boundary. No additional Web-side clarification is required now.

